# NestMate Mobile — Local Environment Configuration
#
# ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
# │  IMPORTANT: This file is GITIGNORED. Never commit it.                  │
# │  Copy this file to .env and edit only your local .env.                 │
# └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
#
# ─── Option A: Let Expo auto-detect the IP (RECOMMENDED — no config needed)
#   Leave everything commented out. When you scan the QR code with Expo Go,
#   the app automatically uses the same IP as the Metro bundler to reach the
#   NestJS backend on port 3000. Works for every teammate with zero config.
#
# ─── Option B: Set a fixed IP (useful for Expo Web / iOS Simulator)
#   Uncomment and replace with your machine's local Wi-Fi IP:
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.xxx:3000
#
# ─── Option C: Deployed backend
#   Set this to your production or staging URL:
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://your-nestmate-api.onrender.com
